    "result_text": "All 21 tests pass across the full suite. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied whenever an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `AddressNormalizer.java` (package-private, mirroring the existing `E164Telephone` pattern): trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Returns `\"\"` for null/whitespace-only input so callers can treat a blank-after-normalization address as absent. Whole-token replacement means \"STONE\" isn't mangled.\n\n**Wiring changes:**\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 normalizes the address, rejects it (400, listed among the offending fields) when blank after normalization, and writes the normalized value back onto the body. This makes the endpoint *store and return* the normalized `address`, since downstream `BuildOwner` maps the published body onto the entity.\n\n2. **`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`** \u2014 the household duplicate check now compares addresses via `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)` on both the request and each existing owner.\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 the shared `householdId` is now derived from, and household members matched by, the `AddressNormalizer` form.\n\nThe test suite (all 12 checkpoints, 21 tests) is green, including the new `Cp12Tests` (whitespace/case, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) and the address-comparison tests `Cp10Tests`/`Cp11Tests`.",
